{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "החול", :translit "ha-chol", :gloss "the profane"} {:he "כובד האבן ונטל החול", :translit "choved ha-even ve-natal ha-chol", :gloss "heavy is the stone and lifted the sand"} {:he "במוצ\"ש", :translit "be-motza\"e-shabat", :gloss "at the departure of Shabbat"} {:he "כובד האבן ונטל החול", :translit "choved ha-even ve-natal ha-chol", :gloss "heavy is the stone and lifted the sand"} {:he "במוצ\"ש", :translit "be-motza\"e-shabat", :gloss "at the departure of Shabbat"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["החול" "כובד האבן ונטל החול"]} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "במוצאי שבת", :spells "במוצ\"ש"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'כובד האבן ונטל החול' appears in Bava Batra 18b as a proverb about circumstances reversing so that the heavy becomes light and the light becomes heavy. The Talmud in BeitZah 16a records that at the departure of Shabbat the additional soul (נשמה יתירה) departs, leaving a person heavy. The concept of an additional soul given for Shabbat and taken at its departure is addressed in BeitZah 12a and Ta'anit 27b.", :sources ["Bava Batra 18b" "BeitZah 16a" "BeitZah 12a" "Ta'anit 27b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יין ושכר", :translit "yayin ve-sheikhar", :gloss "wine and strong drink"} {:he "ולהבדיל", :translit "u-lehavdil", :gloss "and to distinguish"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word adjacency/semichut: ולהבדיל follows יין ושכר in adjacent verses (Leviticus 10:9-10), signaling that havdalah is recited over wine."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah in Berakhot 8:5 records the practice of reciting havdalah over a cup of wine at the departure of Shabbat, and Pesachim 106a discusses whether wine is required for havdalah. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition of 'wine and strong drink' (Leviticus 10:9) with 'and that you may distinguish' (Leviticus 10:10) as an allusion to this practice of making havdalah over wine.", :sources ["Mishnah Berakhot 8:5" "Pesachim 106a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["החול" "כובד האבן ונטל החול"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "החול", :refs ["Proverbs 27:3"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כובד האבן ונטל החול", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "במוצאי שבת", :spells "במוצ\"ש", :letters ["ב" "ש"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "Word adjacency/semichut: ולהבדיל follows יין ושכר in adjacent verses (Leviticus 10:9-10), signaling that havdalah is recited over wine.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:44.120046744Z", :model "glm-5.2"}